{
	"_comment": [
		"UsageFoundry sandbox probe — Docker's default seccomp profile with user namespaces",
		"permitted, and nothing else. Not shipped, not referenced by docker-compose.yml: it exists",
		"for the one throwaway container scripts/sandbox-probe/RUNBOOK.md walks an operator through,",
		"and every claim in it is derived rather than executed. Nothing here has been run.",
		"",
		"Base: moby's own default.json, verbatim, from",
		"  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/moby/moby/v28.5.2/vendor/github.com/moby/profiles/seccomp/default.json",
		"  sha256 01536f1d1df938ae611eba20d6349e0de7a99b6ecdee1549427a0b01b8301e28",
		"byte-identical to profiles/seccomp/default.json at v28.3.3, which is the last tag carrying",
		"it at that path — moby 28.4 moved it into the github.com/moby/profiles module. Your engine's",
		"default is the one that matters and it is not necessarily this one: RUNBOOK.md's first step",
		"is `seccomp-diff.mjs`, which re-derives the base from your own `docker version` and refuses",
		"if anything outside the four blocks below has moved.",
		"",
		"What it widens: clone(2) and unshare(2) when the flags carry CLONE_NEWUSER, and mount(2),",
		"umount2(2) and pivot_root(2) unconditionally. Each of the four appended blocks says why in",
		"its own comment. That is one trade, made once: an unprivileged user namespace grants",
		"CAP_SYS_ADMIN inside itself, and the kernel bugs reachable that way are the reason Docker",
		"blocks the path by default. It is materially smaller than --cap-add SYS_ADMIN, far smaller",
		"than --privileged, and not comparable to handing a container the Docker socket.",
		"",
		"What it does NOT widen, from the same upstream block this borrows three names out of:",
		"bpf, setns, perf_event_open, quotactl, quotactl_fd, syslog, sethostname, setdomainname,",
		"fanotify_init, lookup_dcookie, lsm_get_self_attr, lsm_list_modules, lsm_set_self_attr, and",
		"the whole new mount API (fsopen, fsconfig, fsmount, fspick, open_tree, move_mount,",
		"mount_setattr). keyctl and swapon are not in upstream's profile at all and are not added.",
		"clone3 keeps upstream's ENOSYS, which is what makes glibc fall back to clone. No capability",
		"is granted by this file; --cap-add is a separate flag and RUNBOOK.md passes none."
	],
